
                    ########################################
                    Java JDK and JRE for Building Tinker-FFE
                    ########################################

        This directory contains Java JDK kits downloaded in May 2025 from
        the site:

           https://docs.aws.amazon.com/corretto/latest/corretto-11-ug \
                     /downloads-list.html

        The JDK kits are to be installed prior to building FFE, and are
        needed to run ant scripts and install4j. For building and running
        the FFE, the version used is Amazon Corretto Java 11.0.27.

        On Linux, the provided "deb" or "rpm" file can be used depending
        on the Linux version. On macOS, the provided "pkg" file installs
        the JDK to /Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines. On Windows machines,
        the file provided "msi" file installs the JDK into the directory
        C:\Program Files\Java.

        The "linux", "macos" and "windows" files are JREs constructed by
        using the "Create a JRE Bundle" option from the install4j GUI, or
        the "createbundle" executable included with install4j. These are
        the JREs that will be included in the FFE installation kits.

